id: pm-5p48kf
title: Preserve expected check publishers in PR readiness receipts
description: "CodeRabbit review4315208376 on PR1508 verifies a name-only presence gap: a same-name check from an unexpected publisher disappears from missingContexts even though GitHub CLEAN enforcement still blocks merge. Retain classic and ruleset publisher requirements, prove bound publisher identity from exact-head GitHub check-run metadata, and keep mismatched or unavailable publisher evidence missing without inferring approval."
type: Task
status: in_progress
priority: 2
tags[3]: bug,ci,review
created_at: "2026-10-19T14:58:38.472Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-19T16:20:49.182Z"
assignee: "harness:codex"
claim_principal: "harness:codex#2b1352b8d1f9ffd894ba9de2"
author: "harness:codex"
estimated_minutes: 90
acceptance_criteria: Classic and ruleset publisher bindings survive into the receipt; Matching names from another app cannot satisfy a bound requirement; Unbound legacy contexts retain existing behavior; Exact-head paginated publisher evidence and matching apps are tested without weakening GitHub CLEAN enforcement
parent: pm-obq2
risk: medium
confidence: high
expected_result: Every effective bound check is present only with matching exact-head app evidence; unbound contexts keep their previous behavior and GitHub CLEAN independently gates merge readiness.
dependencies[1]{id,kind,created_at,author,source_kind,author_source}:
