comments[8]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-19T14:58:38.472Z","harness:codex","Duplicate check: complete live203 open and current in-progress lists plus required check publisher search and the full all-status corpus identify no exact active owner. Fresh full predecessor data confirms pm-jm7m3o is completed failure-visibility work and remains closed. This leaf owns the newly accepted review finding at https://github.com/unbraind/pm-cli/pull/1508#discussion_r4315208376 rather than reopening shipped work."
  "2026-10-19T15:04:46.967Z","harness:codex","Accepted CodeRabbit finding has a failing-before control:15 existing watcher tests pass while a wrong-publisher receipt is incorrectly successful. Classic requiredStatusChecks app IDs and ruleset integration_id bindings now survive into requiredChecks. Paginated exact-head check-run metadata proves bound presence; wrong missing and wrong-head apps remain missing, and unbound contexts retain legacy behavior. Focused acceptance separately exercises both policy sources and matching evidence on the second API page. GitHub CLEAN remains independently required for verdict and merge enforcement."
  "2026-10-19T15:07:47.147Z","harness:codex","Final local acceptance:17 watcher tests pass, with focused ESLint and all four TypeScript projects. A live exact-head GitHub negative read on d434018 retains all26 required records including classic Actions Codecov and CodeFactor app identities, correctly keeps only the genuinely absent codecov/patch context missing, and returns failed rather than approving the existing registry-failed head. No GitHub policy merge state or publisher setting was changed."
  "2026-10-19T15:34:32.063Z","harness:codex","Head22b5c7101 full tests pass but the exact global coverage gate reports185/186 helper branches: the sole missing path is requiredChecks ?? [] at line261. Inventory construction always supplies requiredChecks, so the private helper's fallback is unreachable. Remove that redundant branch rather than exporting a test seam or weakening coverage. A scoped helper-only diagnostic confirms the location; its fixed rerun must pass100/100/100/100 before another push. Static quality also correctly rejects missing risk confidence estimate and expected-result metadata on the two newly created leaves. Fill the actual metadata through pm and retain the failed receipts; no assurance threshold changes."
  "2026-10-19T15:37:21.535Z","harness:codex","Fixed helper-only coverage is100/100/100/100:224 statements184 branches48 functions198 lines. The redundant private fallback was removed because inventory construction always supplies the array; coverage scope files thresholds and exclusions remain unchanged. The fixture also includes an unrelated check from the correct app before the second-page match, preserving context-and-publisher identity. Chrome confirms the separate head22b macOS smoke cancellation was hosted-runner acquisition/internal-server failure with no runtime logs. Both old required failures remain evidence for the final exact-head rerun."
  "2026-10-19T15:56:20.791Z","harness:codex",Final-source observability verification is exercising real get/list/contracts reads and this append-only evidence mutation with per-process sampling only. Exact telemetry pairing physical queue state fresh Sentry spans and the required reliability gate will be checked before delivery closure. No persistent telemetry configuration changes are made.
  "2026-10-19T16:17:21.007Z","harness:codex","The complete head775838d review inventory contains a new actionable CodeRabbit finding4315936681: a bound required context may be delivered as a commit status, while publisher evidence currently queries only check runs. This is a real fail-closed liveness bug in the same active publisher leaf, not a reason to weaken publisher checks. Add a discriminated commit-status path whose unavailable publisher identity is explicit and whose acceptance still depends on GitHub CLEAN; preserve exact-head app matching for check runs and regression-test both status and conflicting-name cases."
  "2026-10-19T16:20:49.181Z","harness:codex","Both classic and ruleset semantic negative controls reject the old watcher despite a successful publisher-bound commit status and GitHub CLEAN:2 failures15 passes. The fix discloses status-only bindings as publisherUnverifiable with source commit_status and delegates their publisher enforcement to GitHub CLEAN. A same-name check run still requires exact-head app evidence, including when a status also exists. All17 tests pass and helper-only coverage is100/100/100/100 across237 statements187 branches54 functions206 lines. This is scoped helper evidence, not a substitute for global coverage."
learnings[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-19T15:04:48.551Z","harness:codex",A check name proves presence only for an unbound requirement. Preserve publisher bindings from each effective policy and prove the expected app on the exact head; keep GitHub merge verdict enforcement separate.
